--TEST--
A `return` never leaves a `finally` block, and neither does a `break` whose target lies outside it (`rule:php-migration/no-return-leaves-a-finally`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:php-migration/no-return-leaves-a-finally`: the `return` below would
// replace whatever the region was leaving with — including a throw in flight,
// which no `catch` anywhere in the program would then see. Whether that was
// the intent is a human's call, so the spelling is refused where it is written
// rather than rewritten.
class Reader {
    public function read(): int {
        try {
            return 1;
        } finally {
            return 2;
        }
    }
}

// A `break` is refused on the same grounds when its target is the loop around
// the `try`. The level is read against the loops the block itself opened, so
// the `while` written inside the `finally` keeps its own `break` — that one is
// not reported here.
while (true) {
    try {
        var $n = 1;
    } finally {
        while (true) {
            break;
        }
        break;
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0250]: a `return` never leaves a `finally` block
%A
error[E0251]: a `break` never leaves a `finally` block
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
